368 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1436 0 R
/E (The US generated the highest revenue and profit among the other five countries, reaching around 3.5 million and 699.6 thousand, respectively.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
369 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1437 0 R
/E (The high sales volume in the US was driven by its 4 high-performing stores, each generating over 700 thousand in sales. Meanwhile, other countries operate fewer stores than the US. The UK, Canada, and Germany have 2 active stores, while France and Australia operate 1 only.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
370 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1438 0 R
/E (However, the profit margin percentage of the US was lower than that of the UK and Canada. The UK and Canada achieved margins of 20.75% and 20.06%, respectively, while the US achieved roughly 19.98%.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
371 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1439 0 R
/E (Paris Central generated approximately 725.7 thousand in sales, comparable to several stores operating in the US. Its profit was even higher than that of Chicago Loop, reaching around 144.6 thousand.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
372 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1440 0 R
/E (The single store in France demonstrates better performance compared to each store operating in Canada and Germany, where sales and profits did not exceed 700 thousand and 140 thousand, respectively.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
373 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 211 0 R
/E (Business Recommendations)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
